## Original Content
The world largely moved on from the Rohingya crisis. But the exodus has not stopped, aid is shrinking and a generation of refugees is growing up with little prospect of going home.<br />

## Summary
The Rohingya crisis has entered a dangerous phase nine years on, with the world largely moving on while the refugee exodus continues and aid diminishes. A generation of Rohingya refugees is growing up with little prospect of returning home, highlighting the ongoing humanitarian challenges.

## Key Points
- The world has largely moved on from the Rohingya crisis.
- The exodus of Rohingya refugees has not stopped.
- Aid for the crisis is shrinking.
- A generation of refugees is growing up with no prospect of return.


